@show right nyra
> For several seconds, neither moves.

@page
@panel square | mira | Close-up of Mira, eyes trembling with shock and hurt
MIRA: I thought you were dead.
@panel square | nyra | Close-up of Nyra with a sad, guarded smile
NYRA: Would that have made things easier?
MIRA: You were the one person I thought would never leave me.
@panel wide | nyra, mira | Nyra walking slowly around the pool toward Mira, her black coat trailing, voice soft
> Nyra approaches slowly.
NYRA: I never stopped thinking about you.
MIRA: Then why did you leave with Veyr?

@page
@panel wide | mira, nyra | The sisters face to face in the green light, arguing, intense
NYRA: Because I was tired of watching people suffer while we pretended our little organization could fix everything.
MIRA: Auren believed we could make a difference.
NYRA: Auren believed everyone could be reasoned with.
MIRA: He believed people deserved a choice.
NYRA: And look where that got him.
@panel square | mira | Close-up of Mira's expression hardening into anger
> Mira's expression hardens.
MIRA: Don't speak about him like that.
@panel square | - | Close-up of a single massive stone-plated gauntlet hanging from a leather belt over a dark navy coat with soft pink trim; only the belt and gauntlet are visible, no face
> Nyra looks at Darin's gauntlet attached to Mira's belt.
NYRA: Where is Darin?

@page
@panel wide | nyra, mira | Nyra realizing the truth from Mira's silence, her face falling; Mira looking away
> Mira doesn't answer.
> Nyra understands.
NYRA: I'm sorry.
MIRA: You helped create the world that killed him.
@panel square | nyra | Close-up of Nyra lowering her eyes, guilt and pain
> Nyra lowers her eyes.
NYRA: Come with me. We can still survive this together.
MIRA: I came here hoping you would say something different.

@page
@panel action | nyra | Nyra alone, uncoiling a long whip that drips glowing green venom, her stance turning dangerous
